00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
negative thoughts are like roaches they  ruin everything they are absolutely  despicable and if you don't pay  attention to them they reproduce  exponentially they should be  extinguished off the face of the Earth  but how do you take care of this thought  infestation if you will if first of all  you're not even aware that you have this  problem this is where journaling comes  in as the new year begins many of us  will resolve to adopt new positive  habits to improve or change our lives  and besides reading and waking up early  I can't think of a more life-changing  habit for me than having started to  journal but in the past when I had  thought about journaling I always  pictured the typical my dear diary style  entries and that was just not for me so  today I'm going to share with you 10  different ways that you can use a  journal to actually improve your life so  that you can become a more productive  and positive individual and the best  part is that most of these will take  under five minutes making this the  perfect Habit to start for the new year  first up is morning Pages this is  inspired by the author Julia Cameron and  her book the artist's way morning page  just has been my go-to for years now you  basically take out a pen and paper and I  did say pen because the point is not for  you to obsess over your pristine  handwriting and make sure that you write  everything correctly and have the  perfect grammar it is simply a place  where you can just let go of all of the  random thoughts that you have and all of  the mental clutter that's fogging up  your creative energy as the name  suggests this is done in the morning it  is stream of Consciousness writing  basically you're writing anything and  everything that comes to your mind what  this does is it allows you to just let  go of these things so that you can start  your day with a blank slate and as the  days go by what this also allows you to  do is to be able to see kind of patterns  in your writing maybe you keep writing  down that you should call a particular  friend that might be a hint that you  should do that or maybe you keep writing  down something that had hurt you in the  past maybe that's something you should  address or maybe you keep having the  idea that you should start a particular  project that might be a hint that you  should head in that direction I like to  think of morning Pages like a mental  shower but for your brain so that you  can give your day your best number two  is to write 10 Ideas Daily I love this  one this has definitely been a game  changer for me this is inspired by the  best-selling author James altiter what I  did is I basically got myself a small  Journal where every single day I would  force myself to write 10 Ideas Daily  James alticher describes ideas as planes  flying by and by writing them down  you're giving those ideas a place to  land whether you realize it or not you  get several ideas throughout the day but  we just get so caught up in the busy to  Do's of life that we sometimes don't  even realize this and by writing them  down you're not only making them more  likely that they will actually happen  but you're kind of stretching your  creative muscle if you will whether they  might be life-changing ones or simple  ones like changing the light bulb in the  bathroom for example and the more ideas  that you write down the more creative  you become you are training yourself to  become an individual who sees  opportunities and sees possibilities if  you write down 10 Ideas Daily that's  3650 ideas in a year at least a few of  these have got to be good ones and one  of these could change your life number  three is affirmations positive  visualization and prayer I was a  teenager in early college and I remember  hearing about affirmations and rolling  my eyes and scoffing  like that'll do anything I am personally  a person who believes in the power of  prayer and that the words that you say  and think actually have a direct impact  on your life when you say something like  I'm so stupid or I'm so clumsy your  brain is creating neural connections  that further affirm this belief there  are numerous studies out there that show  that positive visualization can actually  improve physical outcomes because your  brain doesn't know the difference  between imagination and reality think  back to a time when you had thought  about something sad and you started to  actually feel the emotions and made  yourself cry just because of thinking  about that situation that event wasn't  actually happening but your brain didn't  know the difference well thankfully the  same is true for the opposite you can  jot down in a journal visualize what  success actually looks like for you what  it will feel like to accomplish that  goal that you have or how you will  change your life in the future be  detailed about these things where will  you live what will your friends be like  what your future experiences will look  like what your future life will look  like or you can also pretend to be your  older wiser self that's giving you  encouragement and giving you motivation  you can also choose to write hopeful  prayers for things that you would like  to see change in your life whichever  route you decide to take no doubt this  journaling style can be a game changer  for sure because it trains your brain to  be positive and to be kinder to yourself  as well number four is unsent angry  letters oh my goodness this is such a  powerful one I love love love this  journaling style as a child I remember  frequently waking up in the middle of  the night to my parents yelling at each  other and my dad's slamming on the table  right across the trailer wall of my  bedroom growing up in a broken marriage  I did not learn the best communication  skills and though I'm blessed to say  I've been happily married for six years  now I definitely needed to work on my  communication skills because my instinct  was definitely fight or flight and most  of the times I would just kind of hold  things in and let them bother me let  them bother me and then finally explode  but when I heard about unsent angry  letters this was life-changing it  definitely transformed the way that I  communicated not only with my husband  but other people as well what I do with  this is that when I'm upset with  somebody not even just angry but I'm  let's say I'm hurt and I don't know the  particular reason before I go speak to  that individual I write them a letter  that is not meant to be ever sent or  ever be seen you can shred it or burn it  or do whatever you want with it after  it's written the point is to allow  yourself to express the emotion without  covering up any colorful language so  that you can allow yourself to just  release it kind of like a wave that's  rising in the ocean and then allowing it  to fall because when we suppress our  emotions those things eventually will  cause turmoil inside us if we don't just  release it not only that but this allows  you a chance to actually figure out why  this particular thing hurts you and a  way that you can actually speak to this  individual calmly after having gone  through all of these emotions but I  highly recommend this especially for  couples as well because all too often  poor communication leads to separation  number five is simple little quick but  powerful and it is small wins every  night before you go to bed instead of  thinking about all the things that you  should have done all the things that you  procrastinated on all the things that  went wrong that day think about those  small wins this can be something so  simple like I took the stairs instead of  the elevator I finally replaced that  light bulb in the bathroom or I opened  the door for somebody that was coming by  maybe you didn't get everything done  that day maybe it just seemed like a  horrible terrible day where everything  that could go wrong did go wrong but  when you force yourself to write down at  least five things that went right that  day just five little small wins what you  are doing is you're giving yourself more  compassion and forcing yourself to think  of the positive this can allow you to  get a better night's rest and allow you  to wake up tomorrow with more positive  energy before we continue if you like  this video and are getting any value  from it make sure you give it a thumbs  up so that not only can you train your  brain for more positive energy but you  can also train the YouTube algorithm to  give you more positive videos like these  number six is prompted writing I used to  be very critical of this type of writing  because I always envisioned my high  school writing assignments where I had  to write about a particular topic and it  just felt like work but prompted writing  can actually be very fun if you have the  right topics there are many prompted  journals out there but you can also  choose questions of your own the  questions should bring about positive  thoughts and give you a sense of  direction such as what does my dream  life look like what is my ideal self  like what advice would future me have  for myself today or what are some ways  that I could practice more self-care no  doubt prompted writing can fit those of  you who like a more creative style of  writing number seven is the bullet  Journal no list of journaling methods  would be complete without mentioning the  ever so popular bullet Journal bullet  journaling is aimed for personal  organization it's a place where you can  organize and visualize your schedule  your reminders ideas or other to-do's in  a way that suits your creative style it  is not prompted it doesn't have lines on  it it is not clearly defined and that's  the beauty of it you make it work for  you based on what your journaling needs  are you can be as detailed or creative  as you like or as simplified as you like  the bullet Journal is a favorite among  many number eight is words of wisdom or  book quotes through Reading we have the  ability to take knowledge that people  worked for years to obtain and have it  condensed in one book if you haven't  started a reading habit already I highly  recommend you check out my video how to  start a reading habit I'll link that  video down below but if you do currently  read or listen to audiobooks or even  podcasts for that matter a great way to  extract even more information from it is  to have the designated spot where you  can write down key takeaways quotes or  just things that stood out to you this  gives you the ability to not only just  read or even just hear the information  mindlessly but gives you a chance to  actually process and digest the  information and who knows maybe you'll  get some insights of your own number  nine is a gratitude Journal you can  choose to do this either in the morning  or at night or even both this is just  having an area where you can write down  things that you're grateful for and  especially if you're doing this in the  morning you're just kind of starting  your day off right because what you're  doing is instead of waking up thinking  about all the things that you have to do  or all the things that worry or stress  you you're thinking about all the things  that you are grateful for all of the  things that are going right and when you  do this at night is just as powerful  because now you're not keeping yourself  up at night thinking about all those  negative things you're thinking about  the positives allowing you to get a full  nice and peaceful rest number 10 is  ironically the dear diary entry even  though this is not my particular writing  style it may be helpful for those of you  who just want a way to just Express what  you feel what you think or just things  that happen throughout the day it can  definitely be a very healing and  insightful type of writing but I do want  to caution as well that if you are going  through something difficult that it's  always a good idea to find somebody that  you can go to that maybe can guide you  in a positive direction or seek a  counselor so that you're not just kind  of keeping things to yourself if you are  going through something major so these  are the 10 different ways that you can  start a journaling Habit to improve your  life let me know in the comments below  which one would you be starting if you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up and subscribe so you won't miss when  I post a new video I thank you so much  for watching and I'll see you in the  next one bye for now

